\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A scalar trace and a quadratic field expression}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [first-loop trace](fdip-00ZO) is #{4} at
#{U=1}, zero at #{U=\qi}, and #{2} at
#{U=h=(1+\qi+\qj+\qk)/2}, by \ref{fdip-00ZL}.
At #{U=1}, choose any basis #{f_1,\ldots,f_4} of
#{F} and its dual. The paired fields have coefficients
#{\psi_0=\sum_{j=1}^4 f_j\psi_j} and
#{\bar\psi_0=\sum_{j=1}^4\bar\psi_j f_j^*}, so
##{P(1,V)=\sum_{j=1}^4\bar\psi_j\psi_j.}
This is an element of exterior degree two, whereas
#{\trace_F\bbI_F=4} is a scalar. The paired coefficient
functional is needed to turn the former into a number.}
